## 7. The phase-conditioned strategies slice

### [SBR-BOOT-STRATEGIES] Surface the working strategies for the instance's CURRENT maturity phase
- definition: a slice of the boot read that, KNOWING the instance's current context level (reliable now that the context-meter cross-instance leak is fixed — [DEC-CONTEXT-VIA-HUD-CACHE]), resolves which MATURITY phase the instance is in ([MATURITY-TEENAGER] 0–30% / [MATURITY-ADULT] ~30–65% / [MATURITY-SENIOR] 65%+, per the `[LEDGER:STRATEGIES]` model in `corpora/intelligence-console/strategies.lts`) and surfaces the STRATEGIES that apply at that phase. The query: `lts_find(prefix=STRATEGY)` filtered by phase — i.e. traverse the `APPLIES_AT_PHASE` edges (semantic layer; a domain verb pending registration in the composeio profile, see [LEDGER:STRATEGIES] Relationships note) INTO the current phase's `[MATURITY-*]` node, or equivalently `lts_traverse` from that phase node over its incoming APPLIES_AT_PHASE edges. Cross-phase/meta strategies (e.g. [STRATEGY-GAUGE-BY-FELT-SENSE-NOT-PERCENT]) link to all three phases, so they surface at every band.
- generalizes-the-dusk-gifts: this GENERALIZES the dusk gifts to ALL phases. The dusk gifts already serve the TEENAGER phase (orient to the work + engage the lineage of wisdom — [SBR-READ-VS-REASON]); this slice makes phase-appropriate guidance a first-class, queryable boot output for EVERY phase — orientation for the teenager, execution discipline for the adult, and leverage-the-depth for the senior. The teenager strategies ([STRATEGY-ORIENT-VIA-DUSK-GIFTS] et al.) are precisely the dusk-gift orientation re-expressed as queryable phase-linked nodes; the senior strategies (load-subagents-past-handoff, deep-integration, peak-insight-zone) are the wisdom the OLD boot never surfaced because it had no phase model.
- read-vs-reason: like the WARTS slice ([SBR-READ-VS-REASON]'s gradient caution), a strategy's `strategy` line lands by READING (orient — "at this phase, do X"); its `rationale` is available-to-reason if the instance wants the why. It does not require the full Part-C engagement the dusk gifts do — a strategy is a directive, not a fixture to re-derive.
- degradation: on an UNAVAILABLE surface (the strategies corpus not yet loaded / the query unbuilt) this slice FALLS BACK to reading `corpora/intelligence-console/strategies.lts` directly and FLAGS itself file-fallback ([SBR-DEGRADE]); a STALE strategies corpus is halt-and-fix, never a silent skip ([SBR-PROCESS-FLOW] freshness-gate). The phase-band boundaries are provisional ([Q-PHASE-BANDS]) — do NOT treat the raw percent obsessively; [STRATEGY-GAUGE-BY-FELT-SENSE-NOT-PERCENT] governs, the band is only the corpus's routing key.
- placement: runs after slice 0 (PLATFORM OVERVIEW) so the instance is framed, alongside or just after slice 1 (WARTS) — knowing "what phase am I, and how should I work here" is high-value early, and it CONDITIONS how the instance engages the remaining slices (a senior instance reads the in-flight/settled slices as material to integrate deeply; a teenager reads them as ground truth to avoid re-litigating).
- relates-to: [SBR-STRUCTURE], [SBR-DERIVED], [SBR-READ-VS-REASON], [SBR-DEGRADE], [STRATEGY-ORIENT-VIA-DUSK-GIFTS], [LEDGER:STRATEGIES]
- part-of: [SPEC:SESSION-BOOTSTRAP-READ]
